cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "HSM Attestation Reference Implementation"
abstract: >-
  Reference implementation for financial entities operating under DORA
  Article 28(1)(a) and 28(6): a Spring Boot client that submits HSM
  attestation evidence to a supervisory gatekeeper, executes the two-step
  verify/confirm protocol, and retains the cryptographically signed
  supervisory authorisation as the audit record. Version 1.4.0 closes gaps
  found in a second review of the code against its documentation: the
  PKCS#10 request's own signature is now verified (proof of possession),
  the BankID signature is bound to the specific request it authorises, the
  OCSP responder certificate is verified against the issuing CA, the
  Yubico verifier fails closed on a missing capabilities extension, and
  the receipt wire format moves to v2 in lockstep with gatekeeper 1.4.0.
  Version 1.5.0 reads the Yubico capabilities extension big-endian as
  Yubico's reference implementation does, rejects Yubico keys that were
  exported and re-imported, trusts the Test BankID root only when
  explicitly enabled, makes gatekeeper responses deserialisable by the
  HTTP client, registers every configured gatekeeper certificate, and
  sends the configured country code, for deployment together with
  gatekeeper 1.5.0 and railgate 1.5.0. Version 1.6.0 adds Marvell
  LiquidSecurity, Thales Luna, Crypto4A, Fortanix and Entrust nShield as
  verified vendors (nine in all), binds the BankID mandate and the caller's
  transport certificate to the request, limits the age and reuse of BankID
  signatures, verifies the gatekeeper's signed confirm response and checks
  each receipt against what was sent, sends the customer and the technical
  supplier to the gatekeeper (receipt form v3, in lockstep with gatekeeper
  1.6.0), adds a key and CSR signature-algorithm policy and a request size
  limit, and detects every PIT mutant of its production code.
  Companions: gatekeeper (NCA-operated certificate-issuance gate and
  settlement-time signature verification) and railgate (central-bank
  settlement-rail enforcement).
